I would rather call this spell Simulacrum, after the AD&D spell that
does this same thing.  In Nethack, it wouldn't be too unbalanced.  The
only characters that could cast a spell this high level wouldn't be
the combat-oriented characters anyway.  On the other hand, this could
be an effect of a new, very rare scroll, which would allow even combat
classes to create duplicates.
 
The duplicate could be treated like any other tame pet, with the
exception that it and its inventory disappears whenever it would
normally die.

